summary:
  A Cast receiver that says it could not load the stream is reported as one
  that merely did not take it in time.

history:
  A Chromecast or a television answers a stream it cannot load with a
  LOAD_FAILED and a code of its own, and the Cast library hands that to
  whoever listens. The helper did not listen, so every failure read "the
  device did not take the stream within 12s", whether the receiver was
  busy with something else or had tried the address and given up. The
  code goes into the failure line and from there into the journal, so
  that the next television that refuses a station leaves a record of what
  it said. Nothing else is built on it yet.

target:
  package/contents/ui/cast.py

find:
              if watch.failed:

replace:
              if False:

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_cast_play.py::test_a_receiver_that_could_not_load_the_stream_says_which_error.
